   "title": "README — H3 LongTake Image to Video",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 LongTake — Image to Video (+ Refine)\n\n**What it does.** A long video from one picture, clip by clip (124 frames = 5.2 s each), with only one clip in VRAM/RAM: 30 s or 5 minutes cost the same memory, only time (~3.2 min per clip at 0.5 MP on 16 GB). Every clip is written to `output/h3_longtake/<project_name>/` with the audio H3 generates; you can stop, resume (`mode=continue`), redo one clip (`redo_one`) and assemble at the end.\n\n**1. Image to Video**\n- `start_image`: the first frame (keyframe at frame 0). Optional `end_image` = last frame.\n- `prompts`: **one block per clip**, separated by a line with `---`. Block *i* drives clip *i* (0–5 s, 5–10 s, …); the last block repeats. Describe the action of each stretch; the character is fixed by the picture (and by the references), no need to repeat it.\n- Model: **fl2va + Turbo fl2v** without references, or **ref2va + Turbo ref2v** with `identity_reference` (start_image as <Picture 1> in every clip) and/or `face_image` (a close-up as <Picture 2>). Measured over 30 s: no reference → the face drifts to another person by 20 s (ArcFace 0.27); face reference → 0.60.\n- Workflow: `dry_run=true` → check the plan and the clip → prompt table; then `max_clips=1` to check the first clip; then `max_clips=0`.\n\n**2. Refine (second pass, muted: Ctrl+M)** — video \"hires fix\", clip by clip: 0.5 MP → 1.0 MP with `denoise 0.25` (0.4 regenerates more). Adds real skin/hair detail and, with `ref_image_1` + `face_image`, **restores the picture's face on the whole video** even when the first pass lost it (measured: 0.27 → 0.62 over 30 s, seams unchanged). ~5.7 min per clip. Output in `<project_name>/hr` (in the Stitch: `project_name = name/hr`).\n\n**3. Stitch (muted: Ctrl+M)** — assembles the chunks without re-encoding, with the generated audio. Connect its `project_dir` from Image to Video (first pass) or from Refine (second pass).\n\nTips: keep 0.5 MP for the first pass on 16 GB; `context_frames=5` and `seam_match=color` are the measured defaults; steps 4 / Turbo 0.95 — more steps, lower strength or a sigma shift do not reduce grain."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## H3 LongTake — Image to Video (+ Refine)\n\n**What it does.** A long video from one picture, clip by clip (124 frames = 5.2 s each), with only one clip in VRAM/RAM: 30 s or 5 minutes cost the same memory, only time (~3.2 min per clip at 0.5 MP on 16 GB). Every clip is written to `output/h3_longtake/<project_name>/` with the audio H3 generates; you can stop, resume (`mode=continue`), redo one clip (`redo_one`) and assemble at the end.\n\n**1. Image to Video**\n- `start_image`: the first frame (keyframe at frame 0). Optional `end_image` = last frame.\n- `prompts`: **one block per clip**, separated by a line with `---`. Block *i* drives clip *i* (0–5 s, 5–10 s, …); the last block repeats. Describe the action of each stretch; the character is fixed by the picture (and by the references), no need to repeat it.\n- Model: **fl2va + Turbo fl2v** without references, or **ref2va + Turbo ref2v** with `identity_reference` (start_image as <Picture 1> in every clip) and/or `face_image` (a close-up as <Picture 2>). Measured over 30 s: no reference → the face drifts to another person by 20 s (ArcFace 0.27); face reference → 0.60.\n- Workflow: `dry_run=true` → check the plan and the clip → prompt table; then `max_clips=1` to check the first clip; then `max_clips=0`.\n\n**2. Refine (second pass, muted: Ctrl+M)** — video \"hires fix\", clip by clip: 0.5 MP → 1.0 MP with `denoise 0.25` (0.4 regenerates more). Adds real skin/hair detail and, with `ref_image_1` + `face_image`, **restores the picture's face on the whole video** even when the first pass lost it (measured: 0.27 → 0.62 over 30 s, seams unchanged). ~5.7 min per clip. Output in `<project_name>/hr` (in the Stitch: `project_name = name/hr`).\n\n**3. Stitch (muted: Ctrl+M)** — assembles the chunks without re-encoding, with the generated audio. Connect its `project_dir` from Image to Video (first pass) or from Refine (second pass).\n\nTips: keep 0.5 MP for the first pass on 16 GB; `context_frames=5` and `seam_match=color` are the measured defaults; steps 4 / Turbo 0.95 — more steps, lower strength or a sigma shift do not reduce grain."
   },
